Experiment                    : has code 1794205145
Experiment                    : starts at 2026-11-09 07:19:06.592488 (428331.5294513)
Experiment                    : This experiment compares run time and resource consumption of TPC-H queries in different DBMS.
TPC-H (SF=10) data is loaded and benchmark is executed.
Query ordering is Q1 - Q22.
All instances use the same query parameters.
Timeout per query is 1200.
Data transfer volume per query is also measured.
Import sets indexes, constraints, statistics recomputation after loading.
Load durability is relaxed (-xld; restored after the load).
Experiment uses bexhoma version 0.11.13.
System metrics are monitored by a cluster-wide installation.
Experiment is limited to DBMS ['MySQL'].
Import is handled by 8 processes (pods).
Loading is fixed to cl-worker38.
Benchmarking is fixed to cl-worker38.
SUT is fixed to cl-worker36.
Database is persisted to disk of type nvme and size 150Gi. Persistent storage is removed at experiment start.
Loading is tested with [8] threads, split into [8] pods.
Benchmarking is tested with [1] threads, split into [1] pods.
Benchmarking is run as [1, 2] times the number of benchmarking pods.
Experiment is run 2 times.
Maximum DBMS across the whole cluster is 10.
Results are validated against basic correctness requirements.
